  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e5243d49411170e49a1bac6c9ca10949, type: 3}
  m_Name: Passage_Act2_5_MayaCrash
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SundayLastBreath.Data.StoryPassageData
  passageId: Act2_5_MayaCrash
  passageTitle: ACT2 5 MAYACRASH
  associatedRoomId: 
  backdropSprite: {fileID: 0}
  keepPreviousBackdrop: 0
  animatedBackdropFrames: []
  animationFPS: 8
  musicAction: 0
  backgroundMusicOrAmbience: {fileID: 0}
  musicVolume: 0.5
  entranceSFX: {fileID: 0}
  sfxVolume: 0.8
  speakerName: 
  storyText: "/* ====================================================================\r\n   INITIALIZATION & STATE SETUP\r\n   ==================================================================== */"
  narrativeBeats:
  - '/* AUDIO: Heavy rain, engine driving, fading into a blaring car horn */'
  - "RURAL ROUTE 11 \u2014 THE CRASH"
  - /* --- 1. VISUALS --- */
  - "/* --- 2. NARRATIVE --- */\r\n                    You have no destination. Just \"away.\" You took the first rural off-ramp you saw, navigating by the dashboard compass to avoid the major highways. The road is pitch black, winding deep into the dense pine forests."
  - "Then your headlights sweep across shattered glass. \r\n                    \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                                    Deep tire trenches carve through the mud on the shoulder. An official police cruiser is wrapped violently around a massive pine tree. The front end is crumpled like a tin can. The horn is blaring in a continuous, deafening wail."
  - You put the car in park and step out into the freezing rain, drawing your weapon.
  - Vane steps out with you, squinting through the downpour. He raises a hand to block the glaring headlights of the cruiser. "Is anyone alive?" he yells over the blaring horn.
  - "You approach the driver's side. The airbag is deployed, deflated and stained dark. The officer inside\u2014the younger, terrified cop from the Ascott barricade\u2014is violently thrashing against his seatbelt. He is snarling, his jaw snapping wildly at the steel mesh partition separating the front from the back. He's fully turned."
  - From the back seat, you hear terrified, frantic screaming.
  - It's Maya and Lily. The irony is brutal. The cop tried to do a good deed by escorting them out, but he was already infected. Now they are trapped in the back of a police cruiser with a blood-crazed psychopath in the front seat.
  - "/* --- 3. DYNAMIC HUMANITY MONOLOGUE (INTERNAL THOUGHTS ONLY) --- */\r\n                                                                    \r\n                                                                        = 70>>\r\n                                                                            Maya. Lily. The faces from the lobby flash in your mind. The horn is blaring, drawing God-knows-what from the woods right to your position. Every survival instinct tells you to run, but you know you can't leave a child to die in the dark.\r\n                                                                        = 31>>\r\n                                                                            You remember them from the barricade. It's a bad situation. That horn is a dinner bell for every infected lunatic out there. Getting involved means risking your own life, but standing here watching them get torn apart feels wrong.\r\n                                                                        \r\n                                                                            You warned her. She trusted the badge, and the badge drove them into a tree and tried to eat her. You have leverage now. It's a cruel new world, and doing charity work will only get you killed."
  - "/* --- 4. PLAYER CHOICES (THE RESCUE) --- */\r\n                                                                    \r\n                                                                        \r\n                                                                        \r\n                                                                        \r\n                                                                            \r\n                                                                                \r\n                                                                                \r\n                                                                                \r\n                                                                                \r\n                                                                            \r\n                                                                            [+10 HUMANITY] Engage the wreckage and get them out before the noise draws a swarm of them."
  - '[-25 HUMANITY] Tap on the glass. Tell her to pass whatever supplies she has through the crack before you lift a finger.'
  - '[-40 HUMANITY] Get back in your car. It''s too dangerous. They aren''t your problem.'
  - "THE CRASH \u2014 EXTRACTION"
  - You tap the barrel of your weapon against the rear window. Maya looks at you, eyes wide with terror, pleading. You shake your head, pointing at her bag, making a firm 'hand it over' gesture.
  - Her expression shifts from terror to absolute disgust. But she is trapped. She unzips her bag, shoving a handful of supplies through the cracked rear window.
  - "[LOOT ACQUIRED: First Aid Kit, 2x Bottled Water]\r\n                    \r\n                    /* THE FIX: Stop infinite extortion farming */"
  - "You pocket the supplies. Now you have to get them out.\r\n                \r\n                    \r\n                    \n\r\n                    The blaring car horn is deafening. Every second you spend out here is a beacon to anything hiding in the trees. You have to work fast."
  - The rear doors are crumpled and jammed shut. The infected cop is thrashing wildly in the front, his bloody hands squeezing through the steel mesh partition, inches from Maya's face.
  - "i.id === \"Crowbar\")>>\r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                            [CROWBAR] You don't even bother with the cop. You jam the steel under the rear hinges and pop the door cleanly off the frame.\r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            Pry the door open\n\r\n                            [REQUIRES CROWBAR] The frame is bent. You don't have the leverage to force it."
  - "= 2>>\r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                            \r\n                            [MECHANIC] You pop the crumpled hood and rip the battery terminal loose. The horn dies instantly. In the sudden quiet, you easily kick the back window in.\r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            Cut the battery cables\n\r\n                            [REQUIRES MECHANIC / TECH 2] You don't know your way around a wrecked engine block fast enough to kill the alarm."
  - "[VANE] Vane bangs on the driver's side window, drawing the crazed cop's frenzy completely. You safely shatter the rear window and pull them out.\r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            Distract the cop\n\r\n                            [REQUIRES COMPANION] You are alone. There is no one to draw its attention while you work."
  - '[COMBAT] Costs 10 STAMINA. Smash the driver''s window and execute the officer so he stops grabbing at them, then pull them out the front.'
  - "THE CRASH \u2014 AFTERMATH"
  - '/* THE FIX: Stop sound stuttering */'
  - Glass shatters. Metal groans. You haul Maya and Lily out of the wreckage and into the freezing rain.
  - "Maya collapses onto the wet asphalt, clutching Lily fiercely to her chest. She is hyperventilating, soaked in mud and rain, staring at the dead police cruiser. The authority figure she trusted to save her nearly became their coffin.\r\n                    \r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                            \r\n                                \r\n                                \r\n                                    She looks up at you."
  - Her eyes are venomous. "You got what you wanted," she spits, pulling Lily tighter. "Are you going to leave us out here now?"
  - "You gesture to your car. You don't apologize. She doesn't ask you to. It's a transaction now. She climbs into the backseat of your sedan, refusing to speak another word to you.\r\n                                    \r\n                                        Her face does something complicated. The terror washes away, replaced by a profound, heavy realization. You were right. The barricades fell. The system failed. You are the only reason they are alive."
  - '"I''m sorry," she whispers over the rain. "I should have gone with you."'
  - "Vane steps up, offering her a hand. \"We're here now. Come on. Get in the car.\" Maya takes his hand, looking at him with immense gratitude before climbing into the back seat.\r\n                                        \r\n                                            You offer her a hand. She takes it, her grip surprisingly strong. You help her and Lily into the back seat of your car."
  - "[GROUP UPDATED] Maya and Lily are now traveling with you. \r\n                                        \r\n                                        /* THE FIX: Stop infinite party clones & use standard status system */"
  - Before getting back in the driver's seat, you pop the trunk of the ruined cruiser. Inside, you find a locked metal case. You crack it open.
  - "[LOOT ACQUIRED: 10x 9mm Ammo, Police Radio]\r\n                                                    \r\n                                                    /* THE FIX: Stop infinite XP and Trunk Loot farming */"
  - You get back in your car, throwing it into drive. You leave the wrecked cruiser behind in the dark.
  - "RURAL ROUTE 11 \u2014 DRIVING AWAY"
  - You shift the car back into drive.
  - Vane's head snaps toward you. "What are you doing?" he asks, his voice rising in panic. "We have to help them!"
  - Vane stares at you, horrified. He looks at the crashed cruiser in the rearview mirror, hearing the muffled screams, then looks back to your cold, set jaw. He realizes you aren't going to budge. The car rolls forward.
  - "He shrinks back into the passenger seat, pulling his jacket tight. He looks at you like you are the monster. The trust between you is permanently broken. He knows now that if he becomes a liability, you will leave him too.\r\n                    \r\n                    /* Wrapped this logic for code safety/cleanliness */\r\n                    \r\n                        \r\n                    \r\n                    \r\n                \r\n                    You shift the car back into drive. The screaming from the back of the cruiser is muffled by the heavy rain and the blaring horn."
  - You watch in the rearview mirror as the infected cop thrashes wildly against his seatbelt. You tell yourself the glass will hold. You tell yourself someone else will come along. You drive into the dark, and you do not look back.
  dialogueLines:
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: You
    side: 0
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04a95c7136264fc6d4e69cfcfe253bf5, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: Pass the bag through the crack first. Then I'll get you out.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: You
    side: 0
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04a95c7136264fc6d4e69cfcfe253bf5, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: Maya! Cover your faces, I'm going to break the glass!
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
  - introNarration: 
    speakerName: You
    side: 0
    avatarSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04a95c7136264fc6d4e69cfcfe253bf5, type: 3}
    animatedAvatarFrames: []
    avatarFPS: 8
    dialogueText: It's too risky. The cop is infected. If we open that door, we could all die.
    outroNarration: 
    requiresStoryFlag: 
    requiresNotFlag: 
